  "_comment": "FINAL THESIS 120B RE-RUN \u2014 May 1 2026. The May 1 thesis_final sweep had its 48 120B-uring cells OOM-killed because the 'misc anon' was estimated at 108 MiB (20B canonical) but actually measures 232 MiB on 120B (libgomp threadpool + ggml per-thread scratch + io_uring SQ/CQ rings + bsc-pack staging scale with n_layer=36 and n_expert=128). Corrected fixed_anon = 5,280 MiB (KV 4635 + compute eager 413 + misc 232, measured directly from /tmp/smoke_120b_20260501_185202/log_async_experts.txt at decode iter 50 steady state). With 1 GiB transient safety: cache_slots ceiling formula = floor((budget \u2212 3051 pin \u2212 5280 fixed_anon \u2212 1024 safety) / 4.203 slot_bytes) \u2212 4 margin. Yields c693/c1668/c3130/c4592 for 12G/16G/22G/28G. Re-running ALL 24 cells (lazy + mmap_pin too, for clean session-internal baselines that match the same kernel/thermal state as the uring runs). 24 cells \u00d7 3 iters = 72 runs. Multi-topic prompt (no '5000 words', no degenerate-newline collapse \u2014 see project_gibberish_bias). 20B sweep from cgroup_20260501_191023 is COMPLETE and not re-run; only 120B cells in this file.",
